web888-boot (2026.07-3) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * ext4 /boot refactor: the kernel moves from the FAT partition to the
    ext4 rootfs. boot.scr ext4-loads /boot/zImage (a symlink managed by
    the kernel hook) from partition 2; the FAT partition carries only
    boot.bin, boot.scr, uEnv.txt and web888.dtb and mounts at
    /boot/firmware.
  * postinst: install the payload to /boot/firmware; old-layout devices
    (FAT at /boot) fail the guards and no-op safely. Add a kernel-hook
    fallback that creates /boot/zImage when the kernel was configured
    before web888-boot (chroot install order).
  * zz-web888-zimage: manage the /boot/zImage + /boot/zImage.prev
    symlinks instead of copying the kernel onto FAT.

 -- SteamedFish <steamedfish@hotmail.com>  Tue, 18 Aug 2026 13:05:53 +0800

web888-boot (2026.07-2) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Ship web888.dtb in the payload (compiled from config/web888.dts by
    build-boot-deb.sh via write-dtb.sh, no-bootargs variant): image builds
    with DEB_SOURCE=apt no longer download the kernel source tree just to
    recompile the dtb, and on-device apt upgrades now update the dtb too.
  * postinst: install web888.dtb onto /boot with the same temp-file +
    rename + one-generation .bak treatment as boot.bin/boot.scr, guarded
    by the DTB magic (0xd00dfeed).

 -- SteamedFish <steamedfish@hotmail.com>  Mon, 17 Aug 2026 20:20:35 +0800

web888-boot (2026.07-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Initial package (docs/dev/github-ci-apt-repo-research.md §2.8).
    - Ships /usr/lib/web888-boot/: boot.bin (source-built FSBL +
      mainline U-Boot v2026.07 SSBL, packed by build-bootbin.sh uboot),
      the individual fsbl.bin / u-boot.bin components, boot.scr, and the
      default uEnv.txt.
    - postinst configure: on a booted device (FAT partition mounted at
      /boot) updates /boot/boot.bin and /boot/boot.scr via temp-file +
      sync + rename, keeping one-generation backups (boot.bin.bak,
      boot.scr.bak); refuses to write a payload without the Zynq boot
      header sync word. uEnv.txt is installed only when absent — user
      edits (kernel_file overrides) are never clobbered.
    - Skips silently when /boot/boot.bin is absent (chroot/image
      build), so the deb is safe to install during rootfs assembly.

 -- SteamedFish <steamedfish@hotmail.com>  Sun, 16 Aug 2026 00:30:00 +0800
